# c1: spectrum
seg-d9d138bbf716 = A PSD (power spectral density) waterfall of the GNSS L band from the engine's <c1/> kind: frequency across, time down, colour for power above the thermal noise floor. The satellite signals sit below that floor, so what lights up is interference: a chirp jammer, a CW (continuous-wave) tone and narrowband noise. The receiver panel reads each band's <b>C/N0</b> (carrier-to-noise density) and <b>J/S</b> (jammer-to-signal ratio) for the row on show.

# text
seg-59e4f5bc5f17 = <b>kshana</b> spectrum <s1>· l-band-waterfall-jamming.toml</s1>

# attr:aria-label
seg-fa26d7ea085b = L-band waterfall in three zoomed windows, frequency across and time down, newest row at the top. Arrow keys move a cursor over frequency and time; Escape leaves it.

# text
seg-004dc94eb64c = The waterfall is drawn from the recorded run with JavaScript. The engine's report, linked below, shows the same run.

