seg-dd98aa94f8c8 = How often an optical time-transfer link is up when the atmosphere is in the path. For each ground site the engine gives the clear-air loss, the Hufnagel-Valley turbulence state with gamma-gamma scintillation fades and aperture averaging, the availability against the link margin from a stated cloud climate, the ceiling no margin can lift, the outage-duration distribution and the timing error an outage costs a holdover clock. It then shows what extra sites, a larger aperture, another wavelength or adaptive optics buy. The bundled cloud climates are illustrative, not measured; the output is advisory.

