seg-2dc82174942a = For a spacecraft on a sphere (the global shell of the ICG Space Service Volume booklet) or on a Keplerian trajectory from LEO to lunar transfer, counts per constellation (GPS, GLONASS, Galileo, BDS, QZSS, NavIC) and for all together the signals above a C/N0 threshold: availability of one and of four signals, longest outage, received C/N0, dilution of precision, and main-lobe against sidelobe links. Transmit patterns are the booklet's, a parametric stand-in or one you supply; a limb-ray ionosphere, plasmasphere and atmosphere model and a weak-signal receiver design are optional; an onboard GNSS filter for high and lunar-transfer orbits and formation relative navigation are included. MODELLED: compared with the booklet's tables under a pre-registration committed before the run, the minimum-radiated-power constants and the lunar bar agree, the other bars are NOT MET under the pre-registered reading (almost all through the booklet's inconsistent GLONASS beam angle), and the parametric sidelobe stand-in does not reproduce the measured GPS panel patterns.

